<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR short-term rates sharply higher.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR short-term rates sharply higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Short-term Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) rose sharply on Monday after the Central Bank lifted its overnight borrowing rate by seven percentage points to 20 percent, traders said.</p>
<p>The rise in longer term rates was less dramatic as much current higher trend is expected to be temporary, traders said.</p>
<p>The peso was hit by speculation due to the problems in the Thai baht, forcing the Central Bank to raise its key rate several times on Thursday and Friday.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  MAY 19		 MAY 16</p>
<p>    1 W		16  5/16		12</p>
<p>    2 W		14  1/8		 11  5/8</p>
<p>    1 M		12 11/16		11  3/8</p>
<p>    2 M		12  1/16		11  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		11 11/16		11</p>
<p>    6 M		11  5/16		10 15/16</p>
<p>    12M		11  9/16		11  1/16</p>
<p>    VAL		20-May		  19-May</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (63 2) 841-8937</p>
